LearnHarness Fork
================

This program is a modified version of LearnHarness.

Original project: https://github.com/amosblomqvist/learnharness
Copyright: Amos Blomqvist
License: GNU Affero General Public License version 3 (see LICENSE)
Upstream version imported here: 0.5.0 (commit da08cb5f7d098598ba963c6689b22054c9f2a5a3)

The original license, copyright notices, and attribution are preserved.
Modifications in this fork are also under AGPL-3.0-only.

What changed
------------

- Course packs. A course source is a folder of numbered chapter directories,
  each with a Readme.md and optional images. The first preset is
  liquidslr/system-design-notes. The preset is a pointer, not a copy.
- Importer. Reads a local folder, or downloads a GitHub archive at runtime
  into the app data directory (LH_DATA_DIR). Re-runs are idempotent: unchanged
  chapters are skipped; changed chapters are copied again. Review cards and
  linked session ids are kept. Chapters that disappear upstream are marked
  absent instead of deleted.
- Course page at /courses. Chapter status is not started, learning, review
  due, or mastered. Status comes from linked teaching/practice sessions and
  SM-2 cards. The knowledge graph is not a mastery store; a separate flag
  shows when a chapter's notes have propositions in the graph.
- Study and practice open ordinary LearnHarness sessions. The opening message
  quotes the copied chapter file so the existing measure, plan, teach, and
  practice flow can read it. The system-design preset's practice prompt uses
  requirements, estimation, high-level design, deep dive, and wrap-up.
- Reviews use SM-2 (ease, interval, repetitions). Headings in the chapter
  (## ) are separate review cards. There is a today queue. Grades are
  explicit. Practice-session outcomes are not written back into the cards.
- Optional graph extraction calls the existing notes importer for changed
  chapters. It is off unless you ask, because it uses your model.
- External CLI providers. Adds Codex (via `codex app-server`, minimum v0.165.0)
  and Gemini CLI (via `stream-json` and HTTP MCP, minimum v0.68.0) alongside
  Claude Code under Settings -> Providers -> External CLI. All external CLIs
  are off by default (`codex` and `geminiCli` opt-ins), run with built-in tools
  disabled so only LearnHarness tools execute, and delegate authentication and
  billing to the CLI (`CLI billing`).
- Explainer. Adds the `explainer` sub-agent job tool during teaching sessions
  (using the Cheap model slot, toggleable in Settings -> Agent via
  `Tool · explainer`). Bundles `visual-explainer` 0.15.0 (MIT) in
  `src/agent/explainer-kit/` to render self-contained diagram-led HTML pages on
  the server, shown scaled down in a sandboxed card with full-screen view and
  HTML download.
- Fork releases. Sets `appId` to `com.reeschan.learnharness` and `productName`
  to `LearnHarness Fork`, giving the app its own userData directory
  (`%APPDATA%\LearnHarness Fork\data`). Publishes Windows x64 NSIS installers
  (unsigned) on `reeschan/learnharness` GitHub Releases, restricts auto-updates
  to fork Releases, and uses fork versioning (upstream patch * 100 + sequence).

What this fork does not include
-------------------------------

The system-design-notes repository has no license and summarizes a
copyrighted book (Alex Xu, System Design Interview). Its text and images are
not vendored, committed, copied into fixtures, or embedded in prompts.
Tests use short original placeholder chapters under tests/fixtures/course-pack.

Distribution and source
-----------------------

This fork publishes Windows x64 installers on GitHub Releases:
https://github.com/reeschan/learnharness/releases

AGPL-3.0-only applies to the whole application, including all modifications in
this fork. Each release on this fork's GitHub Releases is built from the commit
its tag points to. The Corresponding Source for a release is this repository at
that tag, available from the same Releases page.

Do not redistribute imported notes (such as system-design-notes). Those files
stay in the user's local app data and are not covered by this project's license.

Sync from upstream
------------------

The upstream remote is the public LearnHarness repository:

    git remote add upstream https://github.com/amosblomqvist/learnharness.git
    git fetch upstream
    git merge upstream/main

Do not push to upstream. A local safety setting is:

    git remote set-url --push upstream DISABLE_PUSH_DO_NOT_PUBLISH

Prefer upstream changes outside the fork's files when a merge conflicts.
The fork's additions are concentrated in src/core/course.ts,
src/server/course-import.ts, src/server/course-paths.ts, src/server/courses.ts,
src/store/courses.ts, app/courses, app/api/courses, components/course-pack.tsx,
src/agent/external-cli/, src/agent/codex/, src/agent/gemini-cli/,
src/agent/explainer/, src/agent/explainer-kit/,
src/agent/subagents/explainer-writer.ts,
components/artifacts/explainer-card.tsx, scripts/fork-version.ts, docs/fork/,
README.ja.md, and this NOTICE. After incorporating upstream, follow the fork
versioning rules in docs/fork/release.md.

